  "title": "The Science of Doing Your Best Work",
  "summary": "Steven Kotler is a bestselling author and the executive director of the Flow Research Collective, where he studies the science of peak performance. Most of us have felt it. Hours disappear, everything else fades away, and the work seems to do itself. But what’s actually happening in those moments, and can you make them happen … The post The Science of Doing…",
  "content": "<p>Steven Kotler is a bestselling author and the executive director of the Flow Research Collective, where he studies the science of peak performance.</p>\n\n\n\n<div>\n            <div>\n            <div>\n                <div>\n                                            <div>\n                            <div></div>\n                        </div>\n                                        \n                </div>\n                <div></div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    \n            \n        <div>\n        <h3>Featured clips</h3>\n        <div>\n                                            <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-26-at-14.53.49-300x169.png\" alt=\"What Is a Flow State?\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                00:58                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>What Is a Flow State?</p>\n                                    </div>\n                                                <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-26-at-14.55.14-300x169.png\" alt=\"The Burnout Mistake High Performers Make\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                08:33                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>The Burnout Mistake High Performers Make</p>\n                                    </div>\n                                                <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"168\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-26-at-14.53.06-300x168.png\" alt=\"Why ADHD Can Be a Flow Advantage\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                16:22                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>Why ADHD Can Be a Flow Advantage</p>\n                                    </div>\n                                                <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-26-at-14.53.37-300x169.png\" alt=\"Why Frustration Helps You Learn\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                33:51                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>Why Frustration Helps You Learn</p>\n                                    </div>\n                                                <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-26-at-14.54.57-300x169.png\" alt=\"The Moment Your Brain Learns Best\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                51:13                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>The Moment Your Brain Learns Best</p>\n                                    </div>\n                            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n\n\n<p>Most of us have felt it. Hours disappear, everything else fades away, and the work seems to do itself. But what’s actually happening in those moments, and can you make them happen on purpose?</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Kotler has spent decades studying flow, and he makes the case that it’s far more trainable than most people think. We talk about what brings it on, how hard a task should be before it pulls you in, and why the hobby you gave up as an adult might matter more than you realize.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>We also get into what frustration is really telling you when you’re learning, how play compares with practice, how to focus on work you’d rather not be doing, and how to think clearly when there’s more information than ever and fewer people checking it.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Available Now: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/w_p-68aRdmc?si=n8KhSHk6UEBCJpDw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouTube</a> | <strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/6hwY6OePRF4fPO2faJzoHG?si=zm8lNzCmQfChHVFLkHKmxg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Spotify</a></strong></strong> <strong>|</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/ca/podcast/the-science-of-doing-your-best-work/id990149481?i=1000798332130\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apple Podcasts</a> | <a href=\"https://x.com/shaneparrish/status/2115056297481535953?s=20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">X</a> <strong><strong>|</strong></strong> <a href=\"https://fs.blog/knowledge-project-podcast-transcripts/steven-kotler/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Transcript</a></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>+ Members get the longer, extended version of this conversation, with additional content not included in the public release. Learn more: <a href=\"https://fs.blog/membership/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">⁠⁠https://fs.blog/membership/⁠⁠</a></em></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://fs.blog/knowledge-project-podcast/steven-kotler/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Science of Doing Your Best Work</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://fs.blog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Farnam Street</a>.</p>",
